\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces SoftWall\xspace  architecture for one epoch. (1) Each owner publishes its NeuralRx\xspace  outcome to a decision page. (2) One common-cutoff batch updates the recovery-debt table. (3) The scheduler retimes retained debts around a candidate AI lease. (4) The independent verifier checks the all-fail schedule, credits, and generation, and commits $X'$ or keeps $X_t$. (5) The coordinator publishes each action with its generation and (6) sends the lease with an absolute latest-start. (7) A completion or non-launch marker retires the lease. The shared lane runs retained recoveries in certificate order. The steps are drawn for the evaluated multi-GPU placement (b); the single-GPU placement (a) exchanges IQ, LLR, and TB buffers through CUDA IPC rings and uses the same steps. In (b), cuPHY instance 0 owns TB1--TB3, instance 1 owns TB4 and TB5, and ellipses mark further TBs.}}{7}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overall}{{5}{7}{\sys architecture for one epoch. (1) Each owner publishes its \NRx outcome to a decision page. (2) One common-cutoff batch updates the recovery-debt table. (3) The scheduler retimes retained debts around a candidate AI lease. (4) The independent verifier checks the all-fail schedule, credits, and generation, and commits $X'$ or keeps $X_t$. (5) The coordinator publishes each action with its generation and (6) sends the lease with an absolute latest-start. (7) A completion or non-launch marker retires the lease. The shared lane runs retained recoveries in certificate order. The steps are drawn for the evaluated multi-GPU placement (b); the single-GPU placement (a) exchanges IQ, LLR, and TB buffers through CUDA IPC rings and uses the same steps. In (b), cuPHY instance 0 owns TB1--TB3, instance 1 owns TB4 and TB5, and ellipses mark further TBs}{figure.caption.8}{}}
